how the load balancer decides what requests to pass to which server based on these algos

round robin algorithm:
it passes sequntially 1,2,3 and again 1 and it is good when we have the same soecific hardware configuration for all the servers

weighted round robin:
so based on the ram, lets say we more weight to the first then as it is given more weight we will route twice mpre requests than the server

least connections :

check wjether which server has the more connections and route to the with least live sessions and this one is efficient when we have tasks which may consume variable length of the task time reuired fro completing tasks

